WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.775
Here's gate seven on the
fixtures, after routing both days.

2
00:00:03.775 --> 00:00:07.956
The digest shows sixteen open
notices, eight needing action,

3
00:00:07.956 --> 00:00:13.475
five starting in the next thirty days, two
new, and four closed or no longer listed.

4
00:00:13.475 --> 00:00:16.740
Every action-required notice
shows its due date and the

5
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.075
group it was routed to, which
is the guide's pass condition.

6
00:00:20.075 --> 00:00:21.313
Then the evidence.

7
00:00:21.313 --> 00:00:24.110
Each run folder becomes a numbered record:

8
00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:27.787
the collection, the routing
and the digest, each passing.

9
00:00:27.787 --> 00:00:31.019
The check confirms that
every file matches the hash

10
00:00:31.019 --> 00:00:34.100
list and the three records
form an unbroken chain.

11
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.312
And watch what happens when you
check them as the test stage.

12
00:00:37.312 --> 00:00:40.871
The chain still passes, but
the preflight and the scheduled

13
00:00:40.871 --> 00:00:44.575
run have no passing record, because
on a laptop nobody ran them.

14
00:00:44.575 --> 00:00:48.412
So the go or no-go fails, and
the script exits with an error.

15
00:00:48.412 --> 00:00:51.790
That's the point: the stage
can't pass on a partial run.
